    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5186" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμετά-θετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unalterable, immutable,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάληψις,</span> of knowledge, <i><span class="en">
				Zeno Stoic.
				1.20
			</span></i>; of fate, Chrysipp.ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.264
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.17.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκίνητα καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					331
				</span></i>
			 (Pergam.), etc. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, διακεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.83
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				22.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>not inflected,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				322.1
			</span></i>.</div>
